(Problem Context: An optical transition produces visible red light at wavelength lambda =) Tj
T*
(632.8 nm \(He-Ne laser\). Calculate the ratio of spontaneous emission rate to stimulated) Tj
T*
(emission rate at room temperature \(T = 300 K\). State why population inversion cannot) Tj
T*
(occur in thermal equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Transition Frequency nu and Photon Energy h*nu:) Tj
T*
(nu = c / lambda = \(3.0 * 10^8 m/s\) / \(632.8 * 10^-9 m\) = 4.741 * 10^14 Hz.) Tj
T*
(Photon energy Delta E = h * nu = \(6.626 * 10^-34 J-s\) * \(4.741 * 10^14 s^-1\) = 3.141 *) Tj
T*
(10^-19 J.) Tj
T*
(In electron-volts: Delta E = 3.141 * 10^-19 / \(1.602 * 10^-19\) = 1.961 eV.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Thermal Energy k_B * T at 300 K:) Tj
T*
(k_B * T = \(1.381 * 10^-23 J/K\) * 300 K = 4.143 * 10^-21 J = 0.02586 eV \(~ 26 meV\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute the Ratio \(R_spont / R_stim\):) Tj
T*
(R_spont / R_stim = A21 / \(B21 * u\(nu\)\) = e^\(h*nu / k_B*T\) - 1.) Tj
T*
(Exponent: h*nu / \(k_B*T\) = 1.961 eV / 0.02586 eV = 75.83.) Tj
T*
(R_spont / R_stim = e^\(75.83\) - 1 ~= 8.56 * 10^32.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Spontaneous emission exceeds stimulated emission by 10^32 times at thermal) Tj
T*
(equilibrium! Stimulated emission is completely negligible under normal thermal) Tj
T*
(conditions, proving that lasers require active non-equilibrium pumping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
