([EXAMPLE 2: Threshold Gain Coefficient for a Laser Cavity]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A semiconductor laser has an active cavity length L = 500 micrometers) Tj
T*
(\(0.50 mm\). The internal scattering loss coefficient is alpha_s = 10 cm^-1 \(1000 m^-1\).) Tj
T*
(The cleaved end facets act as mirrors with reflection coefficients R1 = R2 = 0.32.) Tj
T*
(Calculate: \(1\) Threshold gain coefficient g_th, \(2\) If length is doubled to L = 1000) Tj
T*
(micrometers, calculate the new threshold gain.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Formula for Threshold Gain:) Tj
T*
(g_th = alpha_s + \(1 / \(2 * L\)\) * ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \).) Tj
T*
(Mirror product R1 * R2 = 0.32 * 0.32 = 0.1024.) Tj
T*
(ln\(1 / 0.1024\) = ln\(9.7656\) = 2.2789.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Calculate g_th for L = 500 micrometers \(0.050 cm\):) Tj
T*
(Mirror loss term = \(1 / \(2 * 0.050 cm\)\) * 2.2789 = 10.0 * 2.2789 = 22.79 cm^-1.) Tj
T*
(g_th = 10.0 + 22.79 = 32.79 cm^-1 \(3279 m^-1\).) Tj
T*
